Z||000000||afRaceR||01-06-2001||06:34 PM||||I just wanted to tell everyone that I am going to be off the board for a couple of months. Tuesday I fly down to San Antonio to begin my air force basic training.<BR>After that, I go to Keesler AFB in Biloxi for my communications system training. I'll be there for about 6 months w/o my Fiero   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>If there's anyone in the Biloxi area, let me know and we can get together and talk Fiero's. <BR>I just wanted to say that I really appreciate this forum - Cliff for putting this together, and all the forum members for their expert knowledge.<BR>I'll get back on here just as soon as I can gain access.<BR>Thanks again to everybody||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-06-2001||06:54 PM||||Been there, done that. Although after basic, I went to Sheppard AFB for training, Japan for training, Vietnam to work, Mach AFB to  work, then civilian life. A fast 4 year tour. Lots of memories.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Philphine||01-06-2001||08:26 PM||||like comm/nav? i'm in guidance and control and we share a shop with comm/nav. good luck in basic. make joining the last voluteering you do. in basic anyway. don't try to impress anyone, just do what you're told as close as possible. no more and definitly not less. basics not hard, it's just not much fun. tech school is a little better. ||||reg||1
